		{
			"id": "exf7yaBVOBBNPiiNA",
			"description": "Force Staff",
			"local_notes": "Lore: Many psykers prefer a staff to a blade: easier to carry openly as a badge of office, and a familiar focus for channelling telekinetic and biomantic workings. Common across Dark Heresy/Rogue Trader's force-weapon options and depicted for Inquisitorial and Adeptus Astra Telepathica psykers throughout Black Library.\n\nDesign: Same rescaled power-field math as the Force Sword (field on adds +3d and armour divisor (10) over the field-off mundane baseline), applied to a plain hardwood-and-metal quarterstaff (sw+1 cr) instead of an edged blade — a crushing rather than cutting power weapon, with the same charged Force Strike option and scaling note. Handling: weight corrected to 5 lb and min ST to 10 to match the Power Stave anchor exactly (a previous 4 lb/ST 9 quietly drifted lighter than the mundane weapon it's built from). Staff keeps its Basic Set parry 0 with no U, the same exception used for the mundane Power Stave and Shock Staff elsewhere in this project - the skill's own defensive bonus is what a quarterstaff trades raw damage for.",
			"tags": [
				"Melee Weapon",
				"Imperium",
				"Psyker"
			],
			"tech_level": "10^",
			"legality_class": "1",
