		{
			"id": "e5EDY0dwSW1DSXuPl",
			"description": "Force Axe",
			"local_notes": "Lore: A heavier disruption weapon, favoured by psykers who fight as heavily as they cast — seen among Black Templars chaplaincy-adjacent Librarians and some Ordo Malleus interrogators in Black Library material, and offered as a standard force-weapon option in Dark Heresy/Rogue Trader.\n\nDesign: Scaled up from the Force Sword the same way the framework scales chainaxes from chainswords: heavier mundane baseline (sw+2 cut), the same rescaled +3d/armour divisor (10) power-field math (\"+3d over the mundane weapon\"), and a parry penalty for the unbalanced swing. Handling: weight and min ST corrected to 6 lb/ST 12 to match the mundane Power Axe anchor exactly (a previous 5 lb/ST 11 quietly undershot the weapon it's built from). Parry corrected to -1U, the Basic Set Axe/Mace figure this project applies consistently to every one-handed axe (melee.yaml's Power Axe and Chainaxe both carry the same correction) - the previous flat -1 omitted the \"unready after parrying\" half of the penalty.",
