		{
			"id": "eIUNZAJPG2HTP8g3L",
			"description": "Nemesis Force Halberd",
			"local_notes": "Lore: The signature weapon of the Grey Knights: a psychically-attuned halberd that is, to a daemon, as lethal as a bolt round is to a man — Codex: Grey Knights and its Black Library tie-ins (Ben Counter's Grey Knights novels) are consistent on this. Nemesis weapons are built and sanctified specifically to hurt things from the warp.\n\nDesign: Same mundane baseline and rescaled power-field math (+3d, armour divisor (10)) as the Force Axe, reach 1-2 like other polearms, priced and LC0'd as unique Chapter-restricted wargear per the framework's LC table (Astartes/Inquisition-only warp-touched gear). Its Force Strike line waives the normal Perils check as a narrative nod to how routinely and safely Grey Knights use it against their signature enemy, unlike a general-purpose force weapon. Handling: Grey Knights are Astartes, so this halberd is built at Astartes scale rather than the human-scale weight/ST a previous pass gave it (8 lb/ST 12, indistinguishable from a human-carried polearm) - corrected to 14 lb and min ST 14, between the Astartes Chainsword (14 lb/ST 15) and Power Axe (13 lb/ST 18) in this project's melee.yaml, reflecting a two-handed haft weapon rather than a single-handed blade or axe-head. Parry corrected to -1U, the Basic Set convention for a polearm (Halberd-class weapons are unbalanced and slow to recover the same way axes and mauls are) - the previous flat parry 0 undersold how unwieldy a real halberd is on defense.",
			"tags": [
				"Melee Weapon",
				"Imperium",
				"Psyker",
				"Grey Knights"
			],
