		{
			"id": "eYAl7B87HeOQZ8Bw7",
			"description": "Null Rod",
			"local_notes": "A carried or worn Null Rod projects a small, personal anti-psychic field: any Warp Sorcery-tagged ability used, or whose effect would pass, within a yard of the rod must reroll a success as a failure (treat as an automatic Perils of the Warp trigger at -5 to the roll); a psyker touched by the rod itself has their active Warp Sorcery-tagged abilities immediately shut off for as long as contact is maintained.\n\nLore: A grimly plain iron-bound rod, warded and often set with a captive soul-shard, that is anathema to psykers — Inquisitorial and Ecclesiarchy arming-chests keep them for exactly this reason. Widely and consistently depicted across Black Library (interrogators' kit, witch-hunter equipment) and Dark Heresy/Only War's Null Rod rules.\n\nDesign: Modelled as a rules-text effect (the build tool has no \"disable an enemy trait\" feature) rather than a coded bonus, since what it does is binary and narrative: it does not merely penalise a psychic act, it threatens to unmake it. Its own melee stats are a plain, slightly underweight blunt weapon — it is carried as a ward and a badge of office, not a proper weapon, hence sw-1 rather than a full sw+0 mace. Handling: parry corrected to -1U, the Axe/Mace-family convention this project applies to every plain club/mace-class weapon (see the Guardsman's Maul and Shock Maul in melee.yaml) - a rod has no guard and is slow to recover after a swing, the same as any other blunt weapon on this page. Weight (4 lb) and min ST (9) are unchanged.",
			"tags": [
				"Melee Weapon",
				"Imperium",
				"Psyker"
			],
