		{
			"id": "eJJpia-etC4bcZWeg",
			"description": "Psyocculum (Psy-Track)",
			"local_notes": "A worn ocular rig that lets a non-psyker see psychic residue and warp-taint the naked eye cannot: roll vs Optics/Electronics Operation or a relevant Hidden Lore specialisation to spot a hidden psyker, daemon, or recently-used Warp Sorcery-tagged ability's afterglow within 20 yards. Functions as a wearable, skill-based substitute for the Witch- sight advantage, usable by anyone trained on it, not only psykers.\n\nLore: Inquisitorial witch-hunters and Officio Assassinorum operatives use devices exactly like this to track psykers who have no wish to be found — the \"psyocculum\" name and function are best known from Rogue Trader/Dark Heresy-line Inquisitorial wargear lists; Black Library depictions of witch-hunting technology (Eisenhorn's own gadgetry) are consistent with the concept without naming the device.\n\nDesign: Left as a skill-roll rules note rather than a coded feature, since it grants a new use of an existing skill (a sensory check) rather than a numeric bonus — the same approach the build tool's `notes` field is meant for.",
